<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Ulrich von Jungingen</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1360–1410</span></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Ulrich von Jungingen was Grand Master of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/teutonic-order">Teutonic Order</a> from 1407 to 1410. Taking a hard line towards <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/poland">Poland</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lithuania">Lithuania</a> over <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/samogitia">Samogitia</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dobrzyn-land">Dobrzyń Land</a>, he went to war with them in 1409. He was killed on 15 July 1410 at the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-grunwald">Battle of Grunwald</a>, together with much of the Order's leadership, a defeat from which the Order's military power never recovered.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/ulrich-von-jungingen.jpg" alt="Ulrich von Jungingen" width="320" height="372" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: MostEpic · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Arms_of_the_house_of_Jungingen_as_Grand_Master_of_the_Teutonic_Order.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
